  "body": {
    "id": "thm:four-mask-early-kill-negative",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "The answer to \\(\\operatorname{oeq:four-mask-early-kill}\\) is negative under the frozen assumptions. There are allowed fixed primitive radii and a legal equal-share four-mask family \\((P_\\eta)\\), with \\(s(P_\\eta)\\asymp|\\eta|\\) and every local factor restriction of rank two, for which \\(\\mu(P)=0\\) for every law in the model. Hence no alternatives in the same shell can have \\(\\|\\mu(P_{\\eta,d})-\\mu(P_{\\eta,0})\\|_\\infty\\geq c_1|d|\\) for any \\(c_1>0\\) and \\(d\\ne0\\), even though the shells are nonempty.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "eta",
      "Ppath",
      "P",
      "s",
      "d",
      "mu",
      "Mclass",
      "kconst"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:base-model",
      "def:margin-shell",
      "def:four-mask-witness",
      "prop:o3-strict-inclusion",
      "lem:tight-moment-radius-forces-zero-means"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Let \\(q_0=4+\\delta\\), choose allowed constants \\(v_\\star=v^\\star=v>0\\) and \\(M_{\\mathrm{mom}}=(2v)^{q_0/2}\\), and take \\(p_c=1/4\\) with \\(p_\\star<1/4\\). For the four masks, let \\(X_\\eta\\) have rows \\((1,x_t)\\), where\n\\[\n(x_1,\\ldots,x_6)=(1,2,3,4,5,19/5+\\eta),\n\\]\nand put \\(\\Gamma_\\eta=X_\\eta(X_\\eta'X_\\eta)^{-1/2}\\). For sufficiently small \\(|\\eta|\\), all four local restrictions have rank two. Compactness of a small closed \\(\\eta\\)-neighborhood and continuity therefore permit a fixed\n\\[\n0<g_\\star<v\\min_{c,\\,|\\eta|\\leq\\eta_0}\\sigma_2(\\Gamma_{\\eta,S_c})^2.\n\\]\nConditional on every cohort, let \\(\\lambda_i\\) be uniform on\n\\[\n\\{\\sqrt{2v}e_1,-\\sqrt{2v}e_1,\\sqrt{2v}e_2,-\\sqrt{2v}e_2\\},\n\\]\nand set \\(\\varepsilon_i=0\\). Then \\(m_c=0\\), \\(H_c=vI_2\\), and\n\\[\n\\mathbb E\\|\\lambda_i\\|^{q_0}=(2v)^{q_0/2}=M_{\\mathrm{mom}}.\n\\]\nThus all rank, normalization, covariance, orthogonality, homoskedasticity, local-gap, and moment conditions hold. For nonzero sufficiently small \\(\\eta\\), the relation rank is four, so these points are outside the mask relation-rank exceptional set. The proof of \\(\\operatorname{prop:o3-strict-inclusion}\\) gives \\(s(P_\\eta)\\asymp|\\eta|>0\\).\n\nChoose any nonzero sequence \\(\\eta_N\\to0\\) and set \\(s_N=s(P_{\\eta_N})\\). Since a padded projector relation is a contraction, \\(s_N\\leq1\\), and \\(P_{\\eta_N}\\in\\mathcal P_N(s_N)\\), so every shell is nonempty. But \\(\\operatorname{lem:tight-moment-radius-forces-zero-means}\\) applies to every law in this model class, not only to the displayed family, and gives \\(\\mu(P)=0\\). Therefore the requested positive target separation is impossible for every pair of same-shell laws. This falsifies the conjunction in the open-ended question.",
